# M2 IO directed tests (verification plan section 8), pass/fail on W2 and
# W4: the arch harness's chk_io_mon fails a run in which a device access is
# repeated, missing, different from its retired access or left unmatched.
# io_access covers UART byte lanes, store-then-load to a device register and
# the faults of misaligned, AMO, LR and fetch accesses to IO; io_plic claims
# PLIC source 10 (pulsed by the harness) after a wrong-path claim and an older
# store to the same dword. The golden harness serves no device registers.
# Format: <suite>/<name> [budget=<cycles>] [hex=<path>] [tohost=<word index>]
io/io_access budget=100000 hex=test/directed/io_access.hex lockstep=0
io/io_plic budget=100000 hex=test/directed/io_plic.hex lockstep=0 irq=0x400
